  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Philemon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "The gospel changes a servant into a brother.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:1",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And to our beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellowsoldier, and to the church in thy house:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Col. 4:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Col. 4:17.",
            "prettyString": "Colossians 4:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "colossians",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:2",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:3",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:4",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all saints;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:5",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "GR participation, fellowship."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "GR active."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:6",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "For we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "GR affections, compassion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:7",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore, though I might be much bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:8",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:9",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Col. 4:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Col. 4:9.",
            "prettyString": "Colossians 4:9",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "colossians",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 9,
                        "end": 9
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:10",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Which in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:11",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, mine own bowels:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:12",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the gospel:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:13",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "But without thy mind would I do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR assent, suggestion. TG Mind."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:14",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:15",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood.",
            "prettyString": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Brotherhood and Sisterhood",
                "entryId": "tg-brotherhood-and-sisterhood",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:16",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:17",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "If he hath wronged thee, or oweth thee ought, put that on mine account;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "GR something, anything."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:18",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "I Paul have written it with mine own hand, I will repay it: albeit I do not say to thee how thou owest unto me even thine own self besides.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:19",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:20",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Having confidence in thy obedience I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:21",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "2 Cor. 1:11; Philip. 1:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Cor. 1:11; Philip. 1:19.",
            "prettyString": "2 Corinthians 1:11; Philippians 1:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2corinthians",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "philippians",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:22",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Col. 1:7 (7–8); 4:12 (12–13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:23",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellowlabourers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Col. 4:14; 2 Tim. 4:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Col. 4:14; 2 Tim. 4:10.",
            "prettyString": "Colossians 4:14; 2 Timothy 4:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "colossians",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 14,
                        "end": 14
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2timothy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 4,
                    "end": 4,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 10,
                        "end": 10
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Philemon 1:24",
        "book": "Philemon",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
